Neither does http.  Merging will have to be handled by your code.

> Coordinating this likely would require a script to be
> run on the server by the client, which then also
> creates some security considerations.

The client doesn't need to be allowed to trigger
_arbitrary_ actions on the server.  It just needs
to be able to supply data for certain files and
send the server a signal that effectively says
"okay, that's the data, now process it".  In fact,
just supplying the data might be enough -- on
a Unix-type system, it is possible to set up a
daemon that watches for certain files to change
and then does something when that happens.

The remaining security issues, related to
whether the server should trust that the
supplied data are correct, are unavoidable,
given the stated goal.


